b+3 = \frac23\,(a+3).  \tag{2}

Four years ago, Chris’s age was $c-4$. According to the condition, Chris's past age now was $a$:

c-4 = a.  \tag{3}

Equation (3) gives $c = a+4$.

Substitute (3) into (1):

a + b + (a+4) = 27 \implies 2a + b = 23.  \tag{4}

Now, simplify equation (2):

