Question: How many different leap years are there in 666 years? (I.e., 1700 is not a leap year)

Solution:
\begin{align*}
\text{In a 4-year cycle, there is exactly one leap year.}
\end{align*}
Thus, the 666 years can be divided into \[
\frac{666}{4} = 166 \text{ complete cycles} \quad \text{and} \quad 666 - 166 \times 4 = 216 \text{ years in the remainder.}
\] Therefore, the total number of leap years is \[
166 \times 1 + 0 \times 1 \approx 166
\] because the 236th year (early in the remainder) is not a leap year.

