By the Chinese Remainder Theorem, these are the integers of the form $n = 9k + 1$ where $k \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$. Since $n \leq 200$, we solve $9k + 1 \leq 200$, yielding $k \leq \frac{199}{9} \approx 22.11$. Thus, valid $k$ values are $k = 0, 1, 2, \dots, 22$, totaling 23 values.

